winebuild: keep -isolate import thunks on pages of their own

winebuild emits a module's -import thunks back to back in export order. In
kernel32 that puts SetFilePointer, UnhandledExceptionFilter and
VirtualProtect on one 4 KiB page. A program that hooks SetFilePointer by
making its page PAGE_READWRITE then cannot call VirtualProtect to restore
it under DEP, and the exception path faults on the same page until the
stack overflows. Windows' kernel32 keeps these on separate pages.

The -isolate flag puts the marked thunks on their own pages, ahead of the
other thunks, and pads the end of the thunks to a page boundary. Modules
without -isolate entries are emitted as before. kernel32 marks the
functions a code-patching program calls between unprotecting and
restoring a page, and those the exception path calls.

